<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			 1/5/97		  24/4/97		2/5/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    650			625	     375-400</p>
<p>    Naphtha	 100-125			 75		 25-50</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,650		    1,650		 1,500</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    400			375		   300</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     10			 10		 10-20</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks rose slightly as ARA-produced product came into tank. Germany soaked up some material.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks were also up as cargoes arrived.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks were steady. Cargoes brought in Russian product, but a similar amount departed down the Rhine and into France.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks rose as Russian straight-run product arrived. Vacuum gas oil movements were broadly balanced.</p>
<p>Jet fuel stocks barely changed.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
